54,1188,15,11,15,701,16,1106,16119,20912,37,3,44970,15,11,15,701,3741,4080,24,15,1106,12670,362,284,5419,7,16,21,15,701,425,284,5419,7,16,16,15,701,356,284,5419,7,19,15,701,422,284,5419,7,16,15,317,7633,4346,313,35,313,34,313,32,313,33,313,34,317,1502,20912,32,73315,32,49540,1215,2383,20912,33,73315,33,22037,1215,2383,20912,34,73315,34,42125,1215,2383,20912,35,73315,35,42125,317,24157,6405,60,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nIn isosceles triangle $ABC$, angle $BAC$ and angle $BCA$ measure 35 degrees. What is the measure of angle $CDA$? [asy]\nimport olympiad; import geometry; size(125); defaultpen(linewidth(0.8));\ndraw(circle((0,0),1));\ndot(\"$F$\",(0,0),dir(-90));\npair A = dir(160), B = dir(110), C = dir(40), D = dir(10);\ndraw(A--D--C--A--B--C);\nlabel(\"$A$\",A,W); label(\"$B$\",B,N); label(\"$C$\",C,E); label(\"$D$\",D,E);\n[/asy]","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"127b1ffef7a3bdec41382bbd4863df29f19b9f3d483fb27276d96a063b34fcc0"},"seconds":29.23082733154297,"seed":411147293212666043,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the problem and find the measure of angle \\(CDA\\) in the given isosceles triangle \\(ABC\\) where \\(\\angle BAC = \\angle BCA = 35^\\circ\\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Determine the measure of \\(\\angle ABC\\):**\n   Since \\(\\triangle ABC\\) is isosceles with \\(\\angle BAC = \\angle BCA = 35^\\circ\\), the sum of the angles in a triangle is \\(180^\\circ\\). Therefore, we calculate \\(\\angle ABC\\) as follows:\n   \\[\n   \\angle ABC = 180^\\circ - \\angle BAC - \\angle BCA = 180^\\circ - 35^\\circ - 35^\\circ = 110^\\circ.\n   \\]\n\n2. **Identify the cyclic nature of the quadrilateral \\(ABCD\\):**\n   The problem involves a circle, and points \\(A, B, C, D\\) lie on this circle, making \\(ABCD\\) a cyclic quadrilateral. In a cyclic quadrilateral, opposite angles are supplementary (their sum is \\(180^\\circ\\)).\n\n3. **Determine the measure of \\(\\angle ADC\\):**\n   Since \\(ABCD\\) is a cyclic quadrilateral, \\(\\angle ABC + \\angle ADC = 180^\\circ\\). We already know \\(\\angle ABC = 110^\\circ\\), so:\n   \\[\n   \\angle ADC = 180^\\circ - \\angle ABC = 180^\\circ - 110^\\circ = 70^\\circ.\n   \\]\n\n4. **Determine the measure of \\(\\angle CDA\\):**\n   Since \\(\\angle CDA\\) is part of \\(\\angle ADC\\) and considering the cyclic nature and the given points, \\(\\angle CDA\\) is the same as \\(\\angle ADC\\) because \\(D\\) lies on the circle and \\(\\angle ADC\\) is the angle at point \\(D\\) subtended by the arc \\(AC\\).\n\nTherefore, the measure of \\(\\angle CDA\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{70^\\circ}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{70^\\circ}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
